  (text "SAO++ power select: switch common feeds the board. Pos 1 = badge 3.3 V, pos 2 = OFF (pin 2 unconnected)," (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 27.94 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "b234af26-39fe-5220-aa9c-aecb62d009e7"))
  (text "pos 3 = coin cell through D10. Badge supply and cell are on separate contacts, never connected to each other." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 31.75 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "2a6058b1-a63c-54a5-94cb-f8b256065ede"))
  (text "D10 (series Schottky, docs/standard.md section 3): a chip runs from the cell, and an ISP programmer feeds the same rail." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 35.56 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "4b5f89e6-b2df-59fd-8aaa-3d7532ad1712"))
  (text "Maker's circuit (davedarko, Eagle 2017): the ATtiny drives the 9 LEDs of the Y in three rings of three, one pin and one resistor per ring:" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 101.6 165.1 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "b571fd62-ebe2-5b26-8511-1c54395a742a"))
  (text "PB0/MOSI -> D1 D4 D7 (outer), PB1/MISO -> D2 D5 D8 (middle), PB2/SCK -> D3 D6 D9 (inner). Maker's L1..L9 = D1..D9." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 101.6 168.91 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "9ef3edce-352c-5b99-9f45-fe84459fbb68"))
  (text "Resistor values were not recorded by the maker: shared 330 ohm. D1..D9 are on the FRONT (art side) in the maker's positions." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 101.6 172.72 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "d39035be-c014-56aa-8aeb-83e13e74f5af"))
  (text "JP1: the maker's six AVR ISP pads (bare copper, nothing fitted)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 101.6 176.53 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "34cbca2c-b230-509d-bb20-6c1aedf7e98f"))
  (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1")))
